{"name":"Manure","hex":"#ad900d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"manure","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cultivate by manual labor; to till; hence, to develop by culture.","To apply manure (as fertilizer or soil improver)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Animal excrement, especially that of common domestic farm animals and when used as fertilizer. Generally speaking, from cows, horses, sheep, pigs and chickens.","Any fertilizing substance, whether of animal origin or not; fertiliser."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/manure"}],"entries":[{"title":"Manure","blocks":[{"text":"Manure is organic matter that is used as organic fertilizer in agriculture. Most manure consists of animal feces; other sources include compost and green manure. Manures contribute to the fertility of soil by adding organic matter and nutrients, such as nitrogen, that are utilised by bacteria, fungi, and other organisms in the soil. Higher organisms then feed on the fungi and bacteria in a chain of life that comprises the soil food web."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Hestem%C3%B8j.jpg/330px-Hestem%C3%B8j.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manure","wikidata":"Q185716"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Manure_pools_in_Haikou_01.jpg/500px-Manure_pools_in_Haikou_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Manure_pools_in_Haikou_01.jpg/1280px-Manure_pools_in_Haikou_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Manure_pools_in_Haikou_01.jpg/500px-Manure_pools_in_Haikou_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Concrete reservoirs, one new, and one containing cow manure mixed with water. This is common in rural Hainan Province, China.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AManure_pools_in_Haikou_01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/NRCSAR02028_-_Arkansas_%28239%29%28NRCS_Photo_Gallery%29.jpg/500px-NRCSAR02028_-_Arkansas_%28239%29%28NRCS_Photo_Gallery%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/NRCSAR02028_-_Arkansas_%28239%29%28NRCS_Photo_Gallery%29.jpg/1280px-NRCSAR02028_-_Arkansas_%28239%29%28NRCS_Photo_Gallery%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/NRCSAR02028_-_Arkansas_%28239%29%28NRCS_Photo_Gallery%29.jpg/500px-NRCSAR02028_-_Arkansas_%28239%29%28NRCS_Photo_Gallery%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Compost containing turkey manure and wood chips from bedding material is dried and then applied to pastures for fertilizer.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANRCSAR02028_-_Arkansas_(239)(NRCS_Photo_Gallery).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Misthaufen16.JPG/330px-Misthaufen16.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Misthaufen16.JPG/330px-Misthaufen16.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pile of animal manure on a wall","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMisthaufen16.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/ASC_Leiden_-_W.E.A._van_Beek_Collection_-_Dogon_agriculture_05_-_The_women_of_a_neighborhood_ward_with_manure_on_their_way_to_the_field_of_one_of_them%2C_Tireli%2C_Mali_1990.jpg/500px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://t